      "node_id": "kg_doc_9",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Maximillian Oppenheimer (6 May 1902 – 26 March 1957), known as Max Ophüls (] ), was a German-born film director who worked in Germany (1931–1933), France (1933–1940 and 1950–1957), and the United States (1947–1950). He made nearly 30 films, the latter ones being especially notable: \"La Ronde\" (1950), \"Le Plaisir\" (1952), \"The Earrings of Madame de...\" (1953) and \"Lola Montès\" (1955).",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
